---
title: Sync & Repos
order: 5
description: -Sy, -Ss, -Si, mirrorlist, reflector
tags: [pacman, sync, search, mirror, reflector, repository]
---

Searching remote repositories, viewing package info, and managing mirrors.

@code bash
# ---- sync database ----

pacman -Sy                                # refresh package databases
pacman -Syy                               # force refresh (even if up to date)

# IMPORTANT: never use -Sy alone. Always pair with -u or install:
pacman -Syu                               # sync + upgrade (correct)
pacman -Syu package                       # sync + upgrade + install (correct)

@code bash
# ---- search remote repositories ----

pacman -Ss search-term                    # search names and descriptions
pacman -Ss '^vim'                         # regex support
pacman -Ss 'python-.*utils'              # pattern match

@code bash
# ---- remote package info ----

pacman -Si package                        # detailed info from repos
pacman -Si package | grep -E "Repository|Version|Depends"   # filtered

# compare installed vs available version
pacman -Qi package | grep Version         # installed
pacman -Si package | grep Version         # available

@code bash
# ---- repository configuration ----

# /etc/pacman.conf repository sections (Artix)
# Order matters: first match wins

# [system]                                # Artix system (OpenRC-specific)
# [world]                                 # Artix world
# [galaxy]                                # Artix galaxy
# [extra]                                 # Arch extra (via lib32, multilib)

@text
Artix uses its own repos (system, world, galaxy) layered on top of Arch
repos. The Artix repos contain packages patched for OpenRC/runit/s6
compatibility. Arch repos provide the rest.

@code bash
# ---- mirror configuration ----

# Artix mirrors: /etc/pacman.d/mirrorlist
# Arch mirrors: /etc/pacman.d/mirrorlist-arch

# example /etc/pacman.d/mirrorlist
Server = https://mirror1.artixlinux.org/$repo/os/$arch
Server = https://mirror2.artixlinux.org/$repo/os/$arch

@code bash
# ---- reflector: automatic mirror ranking (Arch mirrors) ----

# install
pacman -S reflector

# rank mirrors by speed
reflector --country US --age 12 --protocol https --sort rate --save /etc/pacman.d/mirrorlist-arch

# top 10 recently synced mirrors
reflector --latest 10 --protocol https --sort rate --save /etc/pacman.d/mirrorlist-arch

# verbose with country list
reflector --verbose --country 'United States,Canada' --protocol https --sort rate --save /etc/pacman.d/mirrorlist-arch

# list available countries
reflector --list-countries

@text
For Artix mirrors specifically, use rankmirrors from pacman-contrib instead
of reflector, or manually edit /etc/pacman.d/mirrorlist based on the
Artix mirror list at https://gitea.artixlinux.org/packagesA/artix-mirrorlist/

@code bash
# rankmirrors (pacman-contrib)
rankmirrors -n 5 /etc/pacman.d/mirrorlist.bak > /etc/pacman.d/mirrorlist

@code bash
# ---- adding Arch repos to Artix ----

# install Arch Linux support
pacman -S artix-archlinux-support

# add to /etc/pacman.conf (after Artix repos)
# [extra]
# Include = /etc/pacman.d/mirrorlist-arch

# [multilib]
# Include = /etc/pacman.d/mirrorlist-arch

# then sync
pacman -Sy
